{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515091-drama-or-realism","id":1515091,"title":"Drama or Realism?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-15T03:54:02-07:00","id":1515091,"title":"Drama or Realism?","content":"Because there are some things in VtM where you may go &quot;wait, that's stupid&quot; or &quot;how the <i>fuck</i> does that work??&quot; <br /> But on the other hand, instability and high emotion can lead to fun stories that are worth the suspension of disbelief. Or simply because you think tears of blood is cool or something.<br /> <br /> Like, my limit is vampire &quot;biology&quot;. Their internal organs shrivel up and are useless and they have no body temperature to maintain in order to protect the nonexistent function of their dead organs, but for some reason they sweat. Blood.<br /> There is a sort of narrative purpose in this (when you're stressed or scared the scent of your blood rouses the beast in the vampires around you, alerting them to your fear and making them view you as prey. But it's too silly for me. They can filter blood well enough to produce ocular fluid and saliva, but their <i>useless </i> glands, which clearly serve no purpose other than to sabotage them, weep blood. M'kay. I don't care if it's a curse, this is silly. Tears are a thing along similar themes and let's not even get into the <i>other</i> body fluids replaced with blood (I mean, <i>r e a l l y?</i>))<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I don't care how implausible my political drama is, so long as it's entertaining.<br /> <br /> Are there places where your suspension of belief strains or even snaps in VtM as canon depicts it? And what do you do with those points, alter 'em or ignore them?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T04:45:20-07:00","id":1515097,"title":"","content":"I would have to say my biggest pet peeve with the game is the core design of vampire society, it isn't designed to function, but instead it is designed to promote story hooks.<br /> <br /> Every vampire needs to feed, but for some reason the default is always inferred to be hunting, rather than keeping a herd. It doesn't matter if the kept mortals are willing, enslaved, ghouled, or whatever, from a security standpoint it is just too risky to be constantly hunting.<br /> <br /> Theoretically all vampires are descended from Caine, and his civilization. Yet its not like there is a vampire language which every vampire has to learn once turned. There isn't a shared culture to vampire society, the closest you get is the Traditions, but when you consider the implications of those Traditions, the factions of the Camarilla, Sabbat, and Anarchs would never have arisen if they were actually being enforced on cultural level.<br /> <br /> Even the idea of a city being home to multiple clans/bloodlines is counter intuitive because that just creates infighting and power struggles. If each city was controlled by a given clan exclusively then the power structure would be far more functional. This becomes very important when the idea that shifters are constantly circling the cities trying to keep the vampires contained and occasionally doing raids in an attempt to purge the vampires. Whose is going to be a Harpy when you have guard duty to keep an eye out for a shifter raid?<br /> <br /> Perhaps most egregious of all is the vampire who is more than 50 years old and yet still behaves like a teenager or cartoon villain. Anyone who is that stupid won't survive long in the world of darkness setting. If just a couple years of war changes a person into a hardened survivor, how can a vampire who has survived for centuries place any importance on things as useless as fashion or courtly intrigues of who is sleeping with who? To a certain degree this issue was fixed in Kindred of the East but somehow even with new editions of VtM, centuries old vampires are still behaving like the Lost Boys coterie.<br /> <br /> Lastly there is a complete disconnect between the mechanics of the embrace and the affect it would have on the vampire population demographics. If the setting of WoD is as cut throat and lethal as it is made out to be, then when given the choice between embracing a hyper competent mortal or a random mortal who is hot, no one could waste the resources or time to embrace and raise a neonate who didn't already carry their own weight but give a benefit in addition to that.<br /> <br /> When given the choice between a special forces soldier, a top tier scientist, a fortune 500 company owner, or a random highschooler who lacks experience in anything, why would you ever choose the highschooler except for contrived story reasons or for player options?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T05:32:19-07:00","id":1515103,"title":"","content":"Realism. If it isn't magical, it obeys the sciences<br /> I try to keep things as close to as-written as I can but there's a few times I can't. Of course, reality is often stranger than fiction, so I don't think I lack drama. <br /> <br /> Vampire society is functional-enough. Leaders have a strong tendency towards competence and vampires, despite often being greedy and treacherous, usually have a sense of responsibility to their community. <br /> Vampire fluids aren't all blood because that's silly. Many Vampires are pale but don't exaggerate it and make them all goths. Blush of life is very common, especially as it's the default in folklore, and because if feeding from sleeping people was the only viable option things would be boring: more Casanovas please. <br /> <br /> Vampires just not burning from sunlight is also from folklore, and such a feature would make the masquerade easier, but I think it's a necessary balance feature so I keep it. <br /> <br /> <b>I make a lot of small but significant changes to disciplines to make the masquerade easier. </b><br /> <br /> Obfuscate 1 doesn't make you invisible but makes you and your actions less memorable. You can roll your Obfuscate rating against any investigation against you. Eye witnesses to your violent crimes will remember things wrong, an often reported phenomenon when it comes to high stress scenarios. <br /> <br /> Potence allows you to safely knock people out. <br /> Fortitude protects your clothes when convenient <br /> Presence actually has a table to dictate how much it effects a person. <br /> Thaumaturgy concerning technology is more developed. The Tremere even have a few thaumaturgically advanced AIs that'll scour the internet looking for <s>blackmail</s> incriminating materials while posting red herrings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T06:11:24-07:00","id":1515104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515091-drama-or-realism?p=1515097#post1515097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every vampire needs to feed, but for some reason the default is always inferred to be hunting, rather than keeping a herd. It doesn't matter if the kept mortals are willing, enslaved, ghouled, or whatever, from a security standpoint it is just too risky to be constantly hunting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe<br /> But the idea is, vampires are <i>predators</i><br /> If we take the Caine exist approach, keeping a herd, be a shepperd is more like an Able thing... thus imitating Him wouldn't be... wise<br /> Or simply it is not in the Cainite nature to be shepperd and keep &quot;animals&quot;<br /> And contrary to popular belief, building and maintain a herd is not that easy - especially if you want to cling to your precious Humanity - or what left of it. It is better to accept you are a hunter and eat from faceless nobodies than accept you are a monster who is above Humanity<br /> Not to mention most of the vampires not really had resources or creativity to build a herd/cult/whatever<br /> And most of the time they are not even allowed to do it - a Herd is a potential liability<br /> <br /> Aside these, you are completly right, in a perfect world, especially in the 21st century vampires would have their own little stock of humans not risking the hunt<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515091-drama-or-realism?p=1515097#post1515097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Theoretically all vampires are descended from Caine, and his civilization. Yet its not like there is a vampire language which every vampire has to learn once turned.</div> </div> </div> </div>I beg to differ<br /> Vampirism is not a civilization, but a condition<br /> Every vampire - well except the Nictuku who mostly were monsters to begin with and the Abominations and the Kyasid/Maeghar - were Human and came from the human civlization and cultural background<br /> It is hardly fair to expect unity from the Vampires when Humanity (or any other race in WoD) faild to mastering that...<br /> The closest is the Salubri (well the original idea at leats of them) with the requirement to know Enochian, the Language of the First City - the bit bastarized version of the First Tounge of the Fallen, but the closest to that literally unifiyng language wich is so primodal and strong a Human once hear it, all the other &quot;lesser&quot; languages are basically deleted from its brain\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 06-15-2023, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","tit